252
01:03:01.386 --> 01:03:07.386
For He also says that what is in you makes you clean or unclean.

253
01:03:07.386 --> 01:03:11.386
So then good words will also come out. And that is important.

254
01:03:11.386 --> 01:03:14.386
And it starts with that mindset.

255
01:03:14.386 --> 01:03:19.386
Everything that comes from your hands begins with that mindset.

256
01:03:19.386 --> 01:03:21.386
Otherwise, something else will come from your hands.

257
01:03:21.386 --> 01:03:26.386
What drives us? Is it the love of Christ or something else?

258
01:03:26.386 --> 01:03:30.386
Is it that royal, eternal, pure mindset of Christ?

259
01:03:30.386 --> 01:03:32.386
That is how I have named it today.

260
01:03:32.386 --> 01:03:35.386
So the royal, eternal, pure mindset of Christ.

261
01:03:35.386 --> 01:03:39.386
If this comes up a few times, yes, then I fall into repetition.

262
01:03:39.386 --> 01:03:41.386
That is intentional.

263
01:03:41.386 --> 01:03:44.386
And I want to do that because it is so important.

264
01:03:44.386 --> 01:03:48.386
Because that mindset is royal, it is eternal, it is pure.

265
01:03:48.386 --> 01:03:51.386
And that is what we need.

266
01:03:51.386 --> 01:03:53.386
We have a beautiful text.

267
01:03:53.386 --> 01:03:57.386
Luke 14, verses 25 to 35.

268
01:03:57.386 --> 01:03:59.386
I will take a look for a moment.

269
01:03:59.386 --> 01:04:01.386
I will read it from the NBV.

270
01:04:01.386 --> 01:04:04.386
I hope you can all find it.

271
01:04:04.386 --> 01:04:06.386
Then you can read along with me.

272
01:04:06.386 --> 01:04:09.386
It is so important that you bring your Bible.

273
01:04:09.386 --> 01:04:13.386
If you don't bring your Bible, it's like not bringing your pants.

274
01:04:13.386 --> 01:04:16.386
LAUGHTER

275
01:04:16.386 --> 01:04:18.386
It is so important.

276
01:04:18.386 --> 01:04:21.386
Large people, crowds, followed Jesus.

277
01:04:21.386 --> 01:04:23.386
So I will start reading.

278
01:04:23.386 --> 01:04:26.386
He turned to them and said...

279
01:04:26.386 --> 01:04:30.386
Whoever follows me but does not break with his father and mother...

280
01:04:30.386 --> 01:04:36.386
and wife and children and brothers and sisters, yes, even with his own life...

281
01:04:36.386 --> 01:04:38.386
he cannot be my disciple.

282
01:04:38.386 --> 01:04:46.386
Whoever does not carry his cross and follow me on my way cannot be my disciple.

283
01:04:48.386 --> 01:04:51.386
Well, Jesus, you really ruined the atmosphere.

284
01:04:52.386 --> 01:04:55.386
But this is important, that we realize this.

285
01:04:55.386 --> 01:04:59.386
And I think it is very good to zoom in on this.

286
01:04:59.386 --> 01:05:02.386
I want to read this part because I just think...

287
01:05:02.386 --> 01:05:06.386
you must read everything in the context of what the piece is about.

288
01:05:06.386 --> 01:05:09.386
For which of you, wanting to build a tower...

289
01:05:09.386 --> 01:05:13.386
and does not first sit down to estimate the cost to see if he has enough for the building?

290
01:05:13.386 --> 01:05:18.386
And so you must see if you have enough, otherwise it won't work.

291
01:05:18.386 --> 01:05:22.386
If he has laid the foundation but cannot finish the building...

292
01:05:22.386 --> 01:05:25.386
everyone who sees it will laugh at him and say...

293
01:05:25.386 --> 01:05:29.386
this man began to build but was not able to finish it.

294
01:05:30.386 --> 01:05:34.386
And what king, going out to wage war against another king...

295
01:05:34.386 --> 01:05:36.386
will not first sit down and consider...

296
01:05:36.386 --> 01:05:42.386
whether he is able with ten thousand to meet him who comes against him with twenty thousand?

297
01:05:42.386 --> 01:05:47.386
And if he cannot, while the other is still far away, he sends a delegation and asks for terms of peace.

298
01:05:47.386 --> 01:05:50.386
And so it is with you.

299
01:05:51.386 --> 01:05:54.386
Whoever does not renounce all that he has cannot be my disciple.

300
01:05:54.386 --> 01:05:59.386


301
01:06:00.386 --> 01:06:03.386
And then he says something beautiful, salt is something good.

302
01:06:03.386 --> 01:06:08.386
But if the salt loses its flavor, how can we restore its strength?

303
01:06:09.386 --> 01:06:14.386
It is even no longer useful for fertilizing the ground, so it is thrown away.

304
01:06:14.386 --> 01:06:16.386
So whoever has ears, should listen well.

305
01:06:18.386 --> 01:06:23.386
I want to zoom in on this piece for a moment, especially on the first part.

306
01:06:23.386 --> 01:06:30.386
Because Jesus is really speaking very straightforwardly here.

307
01:06:30.386 --> 01:06:35.386
And there is also a Jewish custom to make something very clear...

308
01:06:35.386 --> 01:06:39.386
they make it really even harder than black and white.

309
01:06:39.386 --> 01:06:42.386
And then that message gets through.

310
01:06:42.386 --> 01:06:47.386
And Jesus spoke like this because he is truly pure.

311
01:06:47.386 --> 01:06:52.386
Here he already begins with his purity. He is pure, so he speaks purely.

312
01:06:52.386 --> 01:06:54.386
And what he says...

313
01:06:55.386 --> 01:06:59.386
Let me see, because then I lose track of it. I printed on both sides.

314
01:06:59.386 --> 01:07:08.386
Jesus says here that he deserves the first place.

315
01:07:08.386 --> 01:07:11.386
But he says it very harshly.

316
01:07:11.386 --> 01:07:16.386
So that means the first place over everything.

317
01:07:16.386 --> 01:07:20.386
Over everything who we are, what we do, and what we have.

318
01:07:20.386 --> 01:07:24.386
So my relationship with him and his authority over me...

319
01:07:24.386 --> 01:07:29.386
must not be determined by the relationships I have with my loved ones.

320
01:07:30.386 --> 01:07:33.386
So the relationship I have with others...

321
01:07:33.386 --> 01:07:37.386
must not determine my relationship with Jesus.

322
01:07:38.386 --> 01:07:41.386
This is really fundamentally important.

323
01:07:41.386 --> 01:07:44.386
And this does not mean that you should not love your family.

324
01:07:44.386 --> 01:07:46.386
Or not take care of your family.

325
01:07:46.386 --> 01:07:48.386
For it is also very clearly stated in the Bible...

326
01:07:48.386 --> 01:07:52.386
if you do not take care of your family, then you are worse than an unbeliever.

327
01:07:52.386 --> 01:07:54.386
And then it will never come.

328
01:07:54.386 --> 01:07:57.386
Says James, brother of Jesus.

329
01:07:57.386 --> 01:08:00.386
So that is in conflict with each other.

330
01:08:00.386 --> 01:08:03.386
And that is very beautiful, because that is the gospel.

331
01:08:03.386 --> 01:08:07.386
It is truly the purifying of His Word.

332
01:08:07.386 --> 01:08:10.386
So what is it about? He must take the first place.

333
01:08:10.386 --> 01:08:14.386
And also your family, your loved ones must give you the space...

334
01:08:14.386 --> 01:08:16.386
to be able to take that first place.

335
01:08:16.386 --> 01:08:19.386
And you must also take that space yourself.

336
01:08:19.386 --> 01:08:23.386
If God asks something of you or if God wants something from you...

337
01:08:23.386 --> 01:08:25.386
then you must be able to take that space.

338
01:08:25.386 --> 01:08:28.386
I love Brecht, really very much.

339
01:08:28.386 --> 01:08:30.386
Not just a little bit either.

340
01:08:30.386 --> 01:08:35.386
But when it comes to God, He must take the first place.

341
01:08:35.386 --> 01:08:39.386
But the other way around, because Brecht loves me too.

342
01:08:40.386 --> 01:08:42.386
What grace.

343
01:08:42.386 --> 01:08:47.386
But when it comes to God, then she is only busy with God...

344
01:08:47.386 --> 01:08:50.386
and then God is more important.

345
01:08:50.386 --> 01:08:55.386
And that is very much of fundamental importance.

346
01:08:55.386 --> 01:08:58.386
He must take that first place.

347
01:08:58.386 --> 01:09:03.386
And it is also true that God loves Brecht and me.

348
01:09:03.386 --> 01:09:05.386
And that is how He intended it.

349
01:09:05.386 --> 01:09:09.386
And He really meant it as that triangle that is often explained...

350
01:09:09.386 --> 01:09:13.386
when you are married, then it is also God and you have each other.

351
01:09:13.386 --> 01:09:17.386
And that is one. But God is indeed the most important.

352
01:09:19.386 --> 01:09:24.386
And it applies to all other family members as well.

353
01:09:24.386 --> 01:09:31.386
Maybe your family is not complete here either. Mine isn't either.

354
01:09:31.386 --> 01:09:35.386
But it is more important that we do the will of the Father...

355
01:09:35.386 --> 01:09:40.386
than that we let the family determine what we do or do not do.

356
01:09:40.386 --> 01:09:46.386
It is important that you come under the authority of your family.

357
01:09:46.386 --> 01:09:50.386
It is extremely important to love your family very much.

358
01:09:51.386 --> 01:09:55.386
With all your heart, all your soul, and all your mind you may love the Lord...

359
01:09:55.386 --> 01:09:58.386
and your neighbor as yourself. That remains standing.

360
01:09:58.386 --> 01:10:03.386
But it is important that when it comes to God, He takes the first place.

361
01:10:03.386 --> 01:10:06.386
And the same applies to our children.

362
01:10:06.386 --> 01:10:09.386
I really love my children very much.

363
01:10:09.386 --> 01:10:16.386
But when it comes to God, it is true that I must put Him first.

364
01:10:17.386 --> 01:10:20.386
And that also applies to our children.

365
01:10:20.386 --> 01:10:23.386
Fortunately, they also love God.

366
01:10:23.386 --> 01:10:27.386
But that relationship remains natural, of course.

367
01:10:27.386 --> 01:10:33.386
However, it is true that God also wants to make that relationship greater.

368
01:10:33.386 --> 01:10:37.386
Better. And that is very beautiful.

369
01:10:37.386 --> 01:10:39.386
And the same applies to our children.

370
01:10:39.386 --> 01:10:44.386
Until they get married, of course. When they marry, they belong to their husband or wife.

371
01:10:44.386 --> 01:10:48.386
And then it is very clear that they may also build that relationship.

372
01:10:48.386 --> 01:10:51.386
As married couples may do.

373
01:10:51.386 --> 01:10:54.386
As God has explained it.

374
01:10:55.386 --> 01:11:01.386
And when He is given that first place, He also sees His love returned.

375
01:11:01.386 --> 01:11:04.386
And He provides for everything we need.

376
01:11:04.386 --> 01:11:09.386
Because He knows what we need. He knows exactly what you and I need.

377
01:11:09.386 --> 01:11:11.386
And He wants to provide in everything.

378
01:11:12.386 --> 01:11:16.386
And actually, in this way, He builds His church.

379
01:11:18.386 --> 01:11:22.386
When we are completely open to Him, He builds His church.

380
01:11:22.386 --> 01:11:25.386
For what happens when we do this in this way?

381
01:11:25.386 --> 01:11:27.386
Then he is a blessing to us.

382
01:11:27.386 --> 01:11:32.386
And we are transformed anew and truly.

383
01:11:32.386 --> 01:11:34.386
A blessing for each other.

384
01:11:34.386 --> 01:11:37.386
If we do not do this, it will go wrong.

385
01:11:38.386 --> 01:11:44.386
And this royal, eternal, pure mindset is truly royal.

386
01:11:44.386 --> 01:11:47.386
He is not harsh, he is not loveless.

387
01:11:47.386 --> 01:11:50.386
It is precisely about preserving and pure love.

388
01:11:50.386 --> 01:11:52.386
This is his covenant.

389
01:11:52.386 --> 01:11:56.386
And a covenant goes much further than an employment contract.

390
01:11:56.386 --> 01:12:02.386
His covenant is truly word for word, man to man, woman to woman.

391
01:12:02.386 --> 01:12:06.386
And if we were not to do this, we would cause harm to God.

392
01:12:06.386 --> 01:12:09.386
We would harm ourselves and we would harm each other.

393
01:12:09.386 --> 01:12:11.386
That is not the intention.

394
01:12:12.386 --> 01:12:17.386
For now, I want to keep it about the relationships, where Jesus talks about relationships.

395
01:12:17.386 --> 01:12:21.386
And then besides that, he also says your own life.

396
01:12:21.386 --> 01:12:30.386
In the text, he even says you must break your own life.

397
01:12:30.386 --> 01:12:32.386
With your own life.

398
01:12:32.386 --> 01:12:37.386
And also my own life is subordinate to my relationship with Jesus.

399
01:12:37.386 --> 01:12:41.386
Not what I want, but what Jesus and the Father want.

400
01:12:41.386 --> 01:12:43.386
This costs me everything.

401
01:12:43.386 --> 01:12:47.386
If I have to make a fool of myself, then this costs me everything.

402
01:12:48.386 --> 01:12:51.386
Except my true identity in Jesus.

403
01:12:51.386 --> 01:12:53.386
It is important to know that.

404
01:12:53.386 --> 01:12:59.386
He wants everything that does not belong to Him to die in me.

405
01:12:59.386 --> 01:13:05.386
He wants me to carry my cross and my dying and suffering, that little share that I may lead,

406
01:13:05.386 --> 01:13:11.386
what I may die, what I may give up, that I carry it for His glory.

407
01:13:11.386 --> 01:13:14.386
And what must die in me?

408
01:13:14.386 --> 01:13:16.386
Good question.

409
01:13:16.386 --> 01:13:19.386
It is not just about my sunny nature.

410
01:13:19.386 --> 01:13:21.386
Of course, that must die too.

411
01:13:21.386 --> 01:13:27.386
But if I do not do what He says, the misery from my sunny nature will anyway be the fruit of my life.

412
01:13:27.386 --> 01:13:32.386
So if I do not walk in His plan, then I stray and I am not there.

413
01:13:32.386 --> 01:13:36.386
The line is thin, the way is narrow.

414
01:13:37.386 --> 01:13:42.386
And I have learned, and I am still learning, to die daily to all my opinions,

415
01:13:42.386 --> 01:13:47.386
all my views, all my intended plans, my own whims, my own wisdom,

416
01:13:47.386 --> 01:13:52.386
my money, my work, my private life, my rightness, to what others think of me,

417
01:13:52.386 --> 01:13:57.386
my sense of honor, my relationships, my family, my friends, my calling,

418
01:13:57.386 --> 01:14:00.386
and my ministry, and even my church.

419
01:14:01.386 --> 01:14:05.386
For I have been bought and paid for by Jesus. I belong to Him.

420
01:14:07.386 --> 01:14:10.386
There is nothing of me in it, outside of Jesus.

421
01:14:11.386 --> 01:14:16.386
And this is what Jesus also means when he talks about the children, become like a child.

422
01:14:16.386 --> 01:14:19.386
He wants to say, everything away.

423
01:14:19.386 --> 01:14:25.386
And I have tried, and I am still learning to do that dying.

424
01:14:25.386 --> 01:14:27.386
There is just nothing of me in it.

425
01:14:27.386 --> 01:14:31.386
Jesus has already bought and paid for everything. It all belongs to him.

426
01:14:32.386 --> 01:14:36.386
And then a lot of problems will fall away from your life.

427
01:14:36.386 --> 01:14:38.386
That is a very nice benefit.

428
01:14:38.386 --> 01:14:41.386
On the other hand, there is also a very important benefit,

429
01:14:41.386 --> 01:14:46.386
is that you are not stuck to anything.

430
01:14:47.386 --> 01:14:54.386
And in the last seven or eight years, I have been able to experience a development in that,

431
01:14:54.386 --> 01:14:56.386
in learning to die.

432
01:14:56.386 --> 01:15:04.386
And that sounds very harsh, but it is really very necessary to learn this,

433
01:15:04.386 --> 01:15:08.386
because the times, as we have already received in the teaching earlier,

434
01:15:08.386 --> 01:15:10.386
are really going to come.

435
01:15:10.386 --> 01:15:12.386
It is going to come.

436
01:15:12.386 --> 01:15:17.386
It is important that you learn to die to everything that you are and what you have.

437
01:15:17.386 --> 01:15:25.386
Because it is important that you focus on Jesus and Jesus alone, that is what it is about.

438
01:15:27.386 --> 01:15:32.386
And everything belongs to him and only in him is it mine.

439
01:15:32.386 --> 01:15:37.386
So it is still mine, but it is in him that it is mine.

440
01:15:38.386 --> 01:15:44.386
For he wants me to be a steward and he wants me to do it his way and how he wants it.

441
01:15:44.386 --> 01:15:48.386
That is the only reason why it can be a blessing.

442
01:15:48.386 --> 01:15:53.386
And only then can he pour himself into me anew every day and fill me.

443
01:15:53.386 --> 01:15:58.386
So if I am not emptied of myself, how can he come in?

444
01:16:00.386 --> 01:16:03.386
That is a very simple conclusion.

445
01:16:03.386 --> 01:16:08.386
If I am just not like an empty vessel that he can fill,

446
01:16:08.386 --> 01:16:13.386
how can that mindset then grow in me? How can it develop?

447
01:16:15.386 --> 01:16:17.386
So I really need to be an empty vessel.

448
01:16:17.386 --> 01:16:22.386
And I need to let him fill me with his royal, eternal, pure mindset.

449
01:16:22.386 --> 01:16:24.386
There you have him again.

450
01:16:24.386 --> 01:16:27.386
And then I will never lose my life.

451
01:16:27.386 --> 01:16:29.386
That is also the promise that he gives.

452
01:16:29.386 --> 01:16:36.386
If I do not hold on to my life, my life, which is not mine, but his,

453
01:16:36.386 --> 01:16:39.386
then I will simply lose it.

454
01:16:39.386 --> 01:16:43.386
But if I let go of that, then I will live.

455
01:16:43.386 --> 01:16:50.386
Because he preserves my life and cherishes me.

456
01:16:50.386 --> 01:16:58.386
Why? We often talk about the inheritance we are to receive in the future.

457
01:16:59.386 --> 01:17:05.386
Do you know whose inheritance belongs to God?

458
01:17:06.386 --> 01:17:08.386
You and me.

459
01:17:08.386 --> 01:17:10.386
Wouldn't you want to cherish that?

460
01:17:10.386 --> 01:17:13.386
Wouldn't you give everything with Jesus?

461
01:17:16.386 --> 01:17:20.386
And then Jesus gives two examples. He has the builder of the tower, the war of the king,

462
01:17:20.386 --> 01:17:26.386
to show that you must clearly realize that you need to know in advance what it costs to follow him.

463
01:17:26.386 --> 01:17:28.386
We must do that calculation.

464
01:17:30.386 --> 01:17:34.386
And then he gives it once more for clarity, as Jesus is,

465
01:17:34.386 --> 01:17:37.386
he would not be himself if he did not give the lesson once more.

466
01:17:37.386 --> 01:17:41.386
So it applies to you as well, whoever does not renounce all his possessions,

467
01:17:41.386 --> 01:17:43.386
cannot be my disciple.

468
01:17:43.386 --> 01:17:47.386
Following Jesus and building his house cost me everything.

469
01:17:47.386 --> 01:17:51.386
But that is not strange and it should not surprise me either.

470
01:17:51.386 --> 01:17:54.386
For it has cost Jesus everything as well.

471
01:17:54.386 --> 01:17:56.386
It has truly cost him everything.

472
01:17:56.386 --> 01:18:01.386
And he was a bit greater and richer and more perfect than I am.

473
01:18:01.386 --> 01:18:05.386
He became sin. He is the purest person in the entire universe.

474
01:18:07.386 --> 01:18:12.386
And he is so pure and we are so corrupt as humans.

475
01:18:12.386 --> 01:18:15.386
And that is why we need him so much.

476
01:18:15.386 --> 01:18:18.386
You know, he hates the sin in us.

477
01:18:18.386 --> 01:18:21.386
He hates the sin in us.

478
01:18:22.386 --> 01:18:26.386
And Gethsemane and Golgotha show the depth of his hatred.

479
01:18:26.386 --> 01:18:29.386
So much does Jesus hate the sin in us.

480
01:18:29.386 --> 01:18:32.386
Why? It destroys us. It makes us corrupt.

481
01:18:34.386 --> 01:18:39.386
And he was made to be sin and corruption, so that I can be clean and pure.

482
01:18:40.386 --> 01:18:44.386
He wants to make this true for each one of us.

483
01:18:45.386 --> 01:18:50.386
Do not think that God would say something and promise something and not do it.

484
01:18:50.386 --> 01:18:55.386
And certainly not this, that would be terrible.

485
01:18:57.386 --> 01:18:59.386
God is a fulfiller of his Word.

486
01:18:59.386 --> 01:19:03.386
Can you see yourself already, clean and pure, as he is?

487
01:19:03.386 --> 01:19:06.386
He was made sick, so that I could be healthy.

488
01:19:06.386 --> 01:19:10.386
He was the richest and has become the poorest, so that I can now be rich in him.

489
01:19:10.386 --> 01:19:13.386
And may be even richer in the future.

490
01:19:13.386 --> 01:19:17.386
He was the most honorable and has been made a disgrace for me.

491
01:19:17.386 --> 01:19:22.386
So that I could be restored in honor and live to his praise.

492
01:19:24.386 --> 01:19:27.386
He had made that calculation long beforehand.

493
01:19:27.386 --> 01:19:29.386
He knew that he was going.

494
01:19:29.386 --> 01:19:33.386
He paid the only true price at the cross of Gogeta.

495
01:19:33.386 --> 01:19:36.386
Through his resurrection and through the ascension.

496
01:19:36.386 --> 01:19:39.386
And by taking his position next to the right hand of the Father.

497
01:19:39.386 --> 01:19:42.386
And for the work that he will still do.

498
01:19:43.386 --> 01:19:45.386
This is that pure love of Jesus.

499
01:19:45.386 --> 01:19:50.386
His royal, eternal, pure mindset was focused on this.

500
01:19:51.386 --> 01:19:56.386
And in this way he has become the true cornerstone and foundation of his church.

501
01:19:56.386 --> 01:20:02.386
And he has chosen that we as humans, we together, as living stones...

502
01:20:02.386 --> 01:20:04.386
may be building blocks for his church.

503
01:20:04.386 --> 01:20:11.386
So your life, my life, may be used as a building block in his church.

504
01:20:12.386 --> 01:20:15.386
The only question is how do we build.

505
01:20:15.386 --> 01:20:19.386
Do we build according to his royal, eternal, pure mindset or not?

506
01:20:19.386 --> 01:20:24.386
Do we build what he wants or do we build something that we have thought of or created ourselves?

507
01:20:25.386 --> 01:20:29.386
Let's take another look at what one of Jesus' best friends has said.

508
01:20:29.386 --> 01:20:32.386
It is the same text that has already been read a few times this morning.

509
01:20:32.386 --> 01:20:34.386
1 Peter 2.

510
01:20:36.386 --> 01:20:39.386
Let's read that with this mindset.

511
01:20:39.386 --> 01:20:41.386
The mindset of Jesus.

512
01:20:42.386 --> 01:20:46.386
It has already been said, so rid yourselves of everything that is bad.

513
01:20:46.386 --> 01:20:48.386
That really includes everything.

514
01:20:49.386 --> 01:20:53.386
All deceit, hypocrisy, all envy, all slander.

515
01:20:53.386 --> 01:20:56.386
And crave like newborn infants.

516
01:20:56.386 --> 01:20:58.386
You see, there is nothing attached to that anymore.

517
01:20:58.386 --> 01:21:03.386
Newborn infants, there is nothing else attached to that.

518
01:21:03.386 --> 01:21:05.386
At most a umbilical cord.

519
01:21:06.386 --> 01:21:11.386
And then we may crave for the purifying of his Word,

520
01:21:11.386 --> 01:21:13.386
the pure milk of his Word.

521
01:21:13.386 --> 01:21:16.386
So that we may grow and attain our salvation.

522
01:21:16.386 --> 01:21:21.386
For you have experienced how pure God is, haven't you?

523
01:21:22.386 --> 01:21:26.386
Join him, the living stone who was rejected by men,

524
01:21:26.386 --> 01:21:29.386
but was chosen by God for his preciousness.

525
01:21:30.386 --> 01:21:35.386
And let yourselves also be used as living stones for the building of a spiritual temple.

526
01:21:36.386 --> 01:21:39.386
Form a holy priesthood.

527
01:21:39.386 --> 01:21:43.386
To offer spiritual sacrifices that are pleasing to God through Jesus.

528
01:21:43.386 --> 01:21:47.386
In Scripture in the Old Testament it is written,

529
01:21:47.386 --> 01:21:51.386
I lay a cornerstone in Zion, which I have chosen for its preciousness.

530
01:21:51.386 --> 01:21:55.386
Whoever trusts in it will not be put to shame.

531
01:21:55.386 --> 01:21:58.386
He is precious to you who trust in him.

532
01:21:58.386 --> 01:22:03.386
But to those who do not trust, the stone that the builders rejected has become the cornerstone.

533
01:22:03.386 --> 01:22:08.386
And it is a stone over which one stumbles, a rock that one strikes against.

534
01:22:08.386 --> 01:22:14.386
And they stumble because they do not obey God's Word; they are destined for this.

535
01:22:14.386 --> 01:22:21.386
It is simply a choice: will I engage with that pure mindset of Jesus, or will I not?

536
01:22:21.386 --> 01:22:24.386
And you see the black-and-white of it here as well.

537
01:22:24.386 --> 01:22:30.386
But the beautiful thing is, as we sit here together, we were once not God's people.

538
01:22:30.386 --> 01:22:32.386
But now we are God's people.

539
01:22:32.386 --> 01:22:37.386
And once God's compassion was not bestowed upon you; it was not ours.

540
01:22:37.386 --> 01:22:40.386
And now his compassion is granted to you.

541
01:22:40.386 --> 01:22:43.386
So actually this is given to us.

542
01:22:43.386 --> 01:22:45.386
It is such a great gift.

543
01:22:45.386 --> 01:22:53.386
And we may be so grateful for it, that we can never be done studying, thinking, and speaking about it.

544
01:22:53.386 --> 01:22:55.386
And what Jesus has done.

545
01:22:55.386 --> 01:23:00.386
Other translations describe it as a royal priesthood.

546
01:23:00.386 --> 01:23:04.386
And that royal aspect is also important, we must not overlook that.

547
01:23:04.386 --> 01:23:08.386
For that royal aspect is what Jesus brings to us anew.

548
01:23:08.386 --> 01:23:14.386
We are meant to be like Jesus, he wants to fill himself with himself.

549
01:23:14.386 --> 01:23:17.386
He is the King of all kings.

550
01:23:17.386 --> 01:23:22.386
And we may be kings, we may be a king's son or a king's daughter.

551
01:23:22.386 --> 01:23:25.386
And that royal thinking is noble thinking.

552
01:23:25.386 --> 01:23:26.386
That is pure.

553
01:23:26.386 --> 01:23:32.386
If you look at pure water, I have talked about that before.

554
01:23:32.386 --> 01:23:38.386
But you also have noble gases, you also have pure metals, which do not rust at all, for example.

555
01:23:38.386 --> 01:23:42.386
And what is important is that we think purely.

556
01:23:42.386 --> 01:23:44.386
And that we adopt that royal aspect.

557
01:23:44.386 --> 01:23:52.386
God is a Father who wants to raise his children, but also wants to explain his dominion.

558
01:23:52.386 --> 01:23:56.386
He wants to show his majesty, so that we can reflect his majesty.

559
01:23:56.386 --> 01:23:59.386
And that we truly walk in his majesty.

560
01:23:59.386 --> 01:24:01.386
He is a great God.

561
01:24:01.386 --> 01:24:07.386
And so we, as his children, may also behave as he is.

562
01:24:07.386 --> 01:24:09.386
And we will read about that shortly.

563
01:24:10.386 --> 01:24:17.386
And the royal aspect of Jesus was expressed, for example, through the washing of his disciples' feet.

564
01:24:17.386 --> 01:24:19.386
What a royal thought.

565
01:24:19.386 --> 01:24:21.386
It is about serving.

566
01:24:21.386 --> 01:24:27.386
It is not about ruling, like I will just wash someone's ears with a thumb.

567
01:24:27.386 --> 01:24:29.386
No, it was about washing feet.

568
01:24:29.386 --> 01:24:35.386
And when we look at the new that God gives, if I come again, as I just explained,

569
01:24:35.386 --> 01:24:42.386
to him and I come as an empty vessel, then he can fill me with that royal thought.

570
01:24:42.386 --> 01:24:45.386
All that is good, all that is pleasing, says the Bible.

571
01:24:45.386 --> 01:24:49.386
That royal thought, I must be impregnated with him.

572
01:24:49.386 --> 01:24:53.386
I must simply, when someone pushes me, have Jesus come out.

573
01:24:55.386 --> 01:24:59.386
And he wants to give insight, he wants us to understand, to comprehend.

574
01:24:59.386 --> 01:25:03.386
He wants us to exhale him.

575
01:25:05.386 --> 01:25:09.386
And when we do that, he simultaneously makes everything new.

576
01:25:09.386 --> 01:25:13.386
If we hold on to it, then it becomes old junk and it starts to stink.

577
01:25:14.386 --> 01:25:19.386
And when we empty ourselves, he fills us anew.

578
01:25:19.386 --> 01:25:23.386
And that applies to everything, everything we are, everything we do.

579
01:25:23.386 --> 01:25:25.386
And then new, pure thinking comes.

580
01:25:25.386 --> 01:25:29.386
New insight comes in the King's domain, there comes new multiplication.

581
01:25:29.386 --> 01:25:35.386
There comes new creation, new creativity, new unity and love for one another.

582
01:25:35.386 --> 01:25:37.386
New love for one another.

583
01:25:37.386 --> 01:25:40.386
New resurrection power in doing and being.

584
01:25:40.386 --> 01:25:44.386
Jesus has given us his resurrection power and he wants to renew that every day,

585
01:25:44.386 --> 01:25:46.386
so that we are transformed.

586
01:25:46.386 --> 01:25:50.386
Constant new restoration, new order in my life.

587
01:25:50.386 --> 01:25:53.386
His creation order is the purpose for my life.

588
01:25:53.386 --> 01:25:57.386
New mysteries, new revelations and much more news.

589
01:25:57.386 --> 01:25:59.386
You are always new with Jesus.

590
01:25:59.386 --> 01:26:01.386
Even if you think, I'm there, then there.

591
01:26:01.386 --> 01:26:03.386
No, it is all new.

592
01:26:03.386 --> 01:26:06.386
It is all new and fresh.

593
01:26:06.386 --> 01:26:09.386
Oh, how beautiful this is.

594
01:26:09.386 --> 01:26:13.386
He is so pure, he is so pure.

595
01:26:13.386 --> 01:26:16.386
And then we move to a piece of priesthood.

596
01:26:16.386 --> 01:26:23.386
And a priesthood is actually bringing people to God and bringing God to the people.

597
01:26:24.386 --> 01:26:31.386
And God has made us all a certain form of stone.

598
01:26:31.386 --> 01:26:33.386
That fits.

599
01:26:33.386 --> 01:26:35.386
And we fit together.

600
01:26:35.386 --> 01:26:37.386
He did that on purpose.

601
01:26:37.386 --> 01:26:40.386
He has also given each of us a unique function.

602
01:26:40.386 --> 01:26:46.386
And yes, that God cares for his creation and that God provides examples in his creation,

603
01:26:46.386 --> 01:26:51.386
I find that so beautiful and I just couldn't help but bring that this time as well.

604
01:26:51.386 --> 01:26:55.386
And I thought, I'm not going to start with little birds, nor with cows, nor with grapes.

605
01:26:55.386 --> 01:26:57.386
I think, I'll take the worm.

606
01:27:00.386 --> 01:27:02.386
And why do I choose the worm?

607
01:27:02.386 --> 01:27:04.386
I can explain that very beautifully.

608
01:27:04.386 --> 01:27:06.386
A worm is a wonderful little creature.

609
01:27:08.386 --> 01:27:12.386
And earthworms, they are truly amazing.

610
01:27:12.386 --> 01:27:14.386
Because do you know what they do?

611
01:27:14.386 --> 01:27:17.386
They sit in the top layer of the earth and then where do they go?

612
01:27:17.386 --> 01:27:18.386
They eat soil.

613
01:27:18.386 --> 01:27:20.386
And they eat compost.

614
01:27:20.386 --> 01:27:24.386
Then you think, eating compost your whole life.

615
01:27:26.386 --> 01:27:27.386
Really, man.

616
01:27:28.386 --> 01:27:30.386
Who thought of that?

617
01:27:31.386 --> 01:27:33.386
And then it comes out again.

618
01:27:34.386 --> 01:27:36.386
And then it is really healthy.

619
01:27:36.386 --> 01:27:38.386
For the whole soil.

620
01:27:38.386 --> 01:27:41.386
And then all those little plants can just grow wonderfully on that.

621
01:27:41.386 --> 01:27:43.386
How beautiful is this?

622
01:27:43.386 --> 01:27:47.386
Oxygen comes in, water comes in, organic substances,

623
01:27:47.386 --> 01:27:50.386
that whole part of the soil life becomes active.

624
01:27:50.386 --> 01:27:52.386
Through that little creature.

625
01:27:53.386 --> 01:27:56.386
And a soil aggregate is formed.

626
01:27:56.386 --> 01:27:58.386
These are actually a bit like clods of earth.

627
01:27:58.386 --> 01:28:02.386
And then you actually have no trouble with erosion.

628
01:28:03.386 --> 01:28:08.386
And if you scoop at home and you have a few little worms in such a scoop,

629
01:28:08.386 --> 01:28:10.386
then you are already doing well.

630
01:28:10.386 --> 01:28:12.386
If you have five in there, then it's like, oh man.

631
01:28:12.386 --> 01:28:14.386
Then everything can grow there.

632
01:28:15.386 --> 01:28:19.386
And I actually want to make a bridge with this.

633
01:28:19.386 --> 01:28:22.386
To what God has for us.

634
01:28:23.386 --> 01:28:26.386
Because we all have a function.

635
01:28:26.386 --> 01:28:28.386
We all have a purpose.

636
01:28:28.386 --> 01:28:31.386
And that one, you are all equally special.

637
01:28:31.386 --> 01:28:33.386
Equally unique.

638
01:28:33.386 --> 01:28:35.386
And God gives leadership.

639
01:28:35.386 --> 01:28:38.386
And He gives ministries.

640
01:28:38.386 --> 01:28:40.386
And He gives gifts.

641
01:28:40.386 --> 01:28:42.386
And He gives function to us.

642
01:28:42.386 --> 01:28:45.386
All so that it fits.

643
01:28:45.386 --> 01:28:50.386
And we may be glad with who we are and what we do and what we have.

644
01:28:50.386 --> 01:28:53.386
For that fits the character that God has given us.

645
01:28:53.386 --> 01:28:57.386
That is truly the most perfect match that can ever be.

646
01:28:58.386 --> 01:29:00.386
And therefore I want to read Romans 12.

647
01:29:01.386 --> 01:29:06.386
For in several places it speaks about the gifts that God gives.

648
01:29:07.386 --> 01:29:09.386
But I also want us to read this together.

649
01:29:09.386 --> 01:29:11.386
I just want to read it together.

650
01:29:11.386 --> 01:29:12.386
Nothing more.

651
01:29:12.386 --> 01:29:19.386
I actually want to keep that eternal pure mindset of Jesus in mind as we read this.

652
01:29:19.386 --> 01:29:22.386
It is actually a joint exercise.

653
01:29:23.386 --> 01:29:29.386
And it is so beautiful to see that the believers together form the body of Christ.

654
01:29:30.386 --> 01:29:31.386
And that is where it starts.

655
01:29:32.386 --> 01:29:34.386
Yes, in the basic Bible.

656
01:29:34.386 --> 01:29:36.386
God is loving and good.

657
01:29:37.386 --> 01:29:41.386
And therefore I encourage you, brothers and sisters, to give yourselves to God.

658
01:29:42.386 --> 01:29:43.386
Then He begins again.

659
01:29:43.386 --> 01:29:47.386
Give yourself as a living and holy offering that God is pleased with.

660
01:29:48.386 --> 01:29:51.386
It is good to serve God in that way.

661
01:29:52.386 --> 01:29:55.386
You must no longer live in the same way as unbelieving people.

662
01:29:56.386 --> 01:29:58.386
But live as new people.

663
01:29:58.386 --> 01:30:02.386
So that you will think in a new way, namely in God's way.

664
01:30:03.386 --> 01:30:05.386
Then you will also live differently.

665
01:30:05.386 --> 01:30:08.386
Wow, feels like a déjà entendu.

666
01:30:09.386 --> 01:30:12.386
Then you will know what God's will is.

667
01:30:13.386 --> 01:30:17.386
And everything that God's will is, is good, is perfect, and is beautiful.

668
01:30:18.386 --> 01:30:23.386
And God has given me the task, Paul, the task to build up your faith.

669
01:30:23.386 --> 01:30:28.386
And therefore I say to all of you, do not consider yourselves more important than you are.

670
01:30:28.386 --> 01:30:30.386
Be humble.

671
01:30:30.386 --> 01:30:36.386
Conduct yourselves in a way that is appropriate to the amount of faith that God has given you at this moment.

672
01:30:36.386 --> 01:30:40.386
And that amount is different for everyone.

673
01:30:40.386 --> 01:30:42.386
You could also say it this way.

674
01:30:42.386 --> 01:30:45.386
Then he will speak differently, a different example.

675
01:30:45.386 --> 01:30:48.386
One body has many parts.

676
01:30:48.386 --> 01:30:52.386
And those parts do not all do the same kind of work.

677
01:30:54.386 --> 01:30:58.386
In the same way, we are all one body with Christ.

678
01:30:58.386 --> 01:31:02.386
We are all different parts of that one body.

679
01:31:02.386 --> 01:31:06.386
And we have all received different gifts from God.

680
01:31:06.386 --> 01:31:09.386
For each gift, God gives us his help.

681
01:31:09.386 --> 01:31:11.386
How beautiful is that?

682
01:31:12.386 --> 01:31:17.386
Whoever has been given the gifts to serve others receives God's help to serve.

683
01:31:17.386 --> 01:31:23.386
Whoever has been given the gifts to teach in the Word receives God's help to teach.

684
01:31:23.386 --> 01:31:24.386
Thank you very much.

685
01:31:24.386 --> 01:31:30.386
Whoever has been given the gifts to encourage other believers in faith receives God's help to do so.

686
01:31:30.386 --> 01:31:31.386
How good he is.

687
01:31:31.386 --> 01:31:37.386
Whoever has been given the gifts to give receives God's help to do so humbly.

688
01:31:37.386 --> 01:31:38.386
Very important.

689
01:31:38.386 --> 01:31:45.386
Whoever has been given the gifts to lead receives God's help to do their utmost in that.

690
01:31:45.386 --> 01:31:51.386
And whoever has been given the gifts to help others receives God's help to do so joyfully.

691
01:31:51.386 --> 01:31:53.386
How beautiful all of this is.

692
01:31:54.386 --> 01:31:57.386
It is so great to see this.

693
01:31:57.386 --> 01:32:03.386
And then Paul moves on, for this is what God has given us.

694
01:32:03.386 --> 01:32:07.386
And then Paul moves on with instructions for us as believers.

695
01:32:07.386 --> 01:32:10.386
And the believers must serve each other and other people.

696
01:32:10.386 --> 01:32:12.386
That is what he is going to tell here.

697
01:32:12.386 --> 01:32:18.386
And then he says, that first sentence of verse 9, is your love must be genuine.

698
01:32:20.386 --> 01:32:22.386
Your love must be genuine.

699
01:32:23.386 --> 01:32:25.386
You cannot fake it with Jesus.

700
01:32:26.386 --> 01:32:28.386
His love is so pure.

701
01:32:28.386 --> 01:32:31.386
And so pure may our love also be.

702
01:32:31.386 --> 01:32:36.386
So hate what is evil and do your best to do what is good.

703
01:32:36.386 --> 01:32:39.386
Hold each other as brothers and sisters.

704
01:32:39.386 --> 01:32:43.386
Show each other that you have respect for one another.

705
01:32:43.386 --> 01:32:46.386
And be an example for each other in this.

706
01:32:47.386 --> 01:32:51.386
Do not be lazy in serving the Lord, but serve Him with zeal.

707
01:32:52.386 --> 01:32:55.386
Be joyful about the things that are yet to come.

708
01:32:55.386 --> 01:32:58.386
And be patient when you are persecuted.

709
01:32:58.386 --> 01:33:01.386
And never stop praying.

710
01:33:02.386 --> 01:33:05.386
Give to the believers what they need.

711
01:33:05.386 --> 01:33:07.386
Be hospitable.

712
01:33:07.386 --> 01:33:12.386
Bless the people by whom you are persecuted and do not curse them.

713
01:33:13.386 --> 01:33:17.386
Empathize with others whether they are happy or sad.

714
01:33:17.386 --> 01:33:19.386
Be one with each other.

715
01:33:19.386 --> 01:33:23.386
When we are completely stripped of everything we are,

716
01:33:23.386 --> 01:33:26.386
it is so simple to be one with each other.

717
01:33:26.386 --> 01:33:28.386
For then Jesus is alone.

718
01:33:29.386 --> 01:33:34.386
Do not long for increasingly important tasks, but also be content with simple tasks.

719
01:33:34.386 --> 01:33:37.386
Thank you, Inge, for the task you are doing.

720
01:33:40.386 --> 01:33:42.386
Do not be stubborn.

721
01:33:42.386 --> 01:33:47.386
If someone does you harm, do not repay evil for evil.

722
01:33:47.386 --> 01:33:49.386
Be good to everyone.

723
01:33:49.386 --> 01:33:54.386
Also do your best to live in peace with all people as much as possible.

724
01:33:55.386 --> 01:34:00.386
Do not take revenge on people for what they do to you, but leave it to God.

725
01:34:00.386 --> 01:34:02.386
For it is written in the books.

726
01:34:02.386 --> 01:34:04.386
Leave it to me to take revenge.

727
01:34:04.386 --> 01:34:07.386
I will give them what they deserve, says the Lord.

728
01:34:07.386 --> 01:34:09.386
So we do not have to do that.

729
01:34:09.386 --> 01:34:12.386
Well, that already saves a lot of misery.

730
01:34:12.386 --> 01:34:16.386
So if your enemy is hungry, feed him.

731
01:34:16.386 --> 01:34:19.386
And if he is thirsty, give him something to drink.

732
01:34:19.386 --> 01:34:24.386
For in doing so, he will feel deep shame for the evil he has done.

733
01:34:24.386 --> 01:34:28.386
Do not be overcome by evil, but overcome evil with good.

734
01:34:29.386 --> 01:34:34.386
Thus far the advice, also regarding our priestly work.

735
01:34:34.386 --> 01:34:39.386
This is also the mindset, but also the instructions for the priestly work that we are allowed to do.

736
01:34:39.386 --> 01:34:41.386
The spiritual sacrifices that we are allowed to bring.

737
01:34:41.386 --> 01:34:48.386
When we look at the older translations, Romans 12 is initially spoken of as reasonable worship.

738
01:34:48.386 --> 01:34:51.386
This is who we may be and what we may do.

739
01:34:53.386 --> 01:35:01.386
